        "original_id": "ee1c8c58-6d7c-57e5-a930-6075b1ec702c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Éluard, Georges Bataille, Laurence Bataille, Sylvia Bataille\n- Works: Capitale de la douleur\n- Roles: poet, intellectual, literary figure, writer, actress\n- Concepts: surrealist movement\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Éluard was born as Eugène Émile Paul Grindel on 14 December 1895 and died on 18 November 1952.\n- Georges Bataille was born as Georges Albert Maurice Victor Bataille on 10 September 1897 and died on 9 July 1962.\n- Paul Éluard was a French poet and one of the founders of the surrealist movement.\n- Georges Bataille was a French intellectual and literary figure who worked in literature, philosophy, anthropology, economics, sociology, and history of art.\n- Capitale de la douleur is a book of poems by French surrealist poet Paul Éluard.\n- Laurence Bataille was the only daughter of writer Georges Bataille and actress Sylvia Bataille.",
